    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d773">

                <pb facs="0872" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/10245</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Director of the Bureau of Enemy Trade, War Trade Board</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">McGonigal</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your inquiry of June 1,
                        1918,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d773-f1"/> the Department begs to inform you that
                    for purposes of the dispatch of postal correspondence and the remittance of
                    funds, Roumania should be regarded, for the present, as territory occupied by
                    the enemy. For your information, I may add that there is no consular office of
                    the United States in Roumania at present.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
